# Task X – Advanced SQL Query System

## Objective
Implement subqueries and nested queries to perform advanced product, customer, and business analysis using the existing Customer, Product, Orders, and Payment tables.

## SQL Queries

### 1. Products Above Average Price
Find products whose price is greater than the average price of all products.

```sql
USE DBMS;

SELECT
    Product_ID,
    Product_Name,
    Price,
    Category
FROM Product
WHERE Price > (
    SELECT AVG(Price)
    FROM Product
)
ORDER BY Price DESC;
```

### 2. Customers with Maximum Purchases
Find the customer or customers whose total paid purchase amount is the highest. The nested query also handles ties.

```sql
SELECT
    c.Customer_ID,
    c.Customer_Name,
    SUM(p.Payment_Amount) AS Total_Purchase
FROM Customer c
INNER JOIN Orders o
    ON c.Customer_ID = o.Customer_ID
INNER JOIN Payment p
    ON o.Order_ID = p.Order_ID
WHERE p.Payment_Status = 'Paid'
GROUP BY c.Customer_ID, c.Customer_Name
HAVING SUM(p.Payment_Amount) = (
    SELECT MAX(Customer_Total)
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUM(p2.Payment_Amount) AS Customer_Total
        FROM Orders o2
        INNER JOIN Payment p2
            ON o2.Order_ID = p2.Order_ID
        WHERE p2.Payment_Status = 'Paid'
        GROUP BY o2.Customer_ID
    ) AS Customer_Purchases
);
```

### 3. Products That Have Been Purchased
Use the EXISTS operator with a correlated subquery to list products that have at least one order.

```sql
SELECT
    p.Product_ID,
    p.Product_Name,
    p.Price,
    p.Category
FROM Product p
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM Orders o
    WHERE o.Product_ID = p.Product_ID
);
```

### 4. Customers Spending Above the Average Customer Purchase
Find customers whose total paid purchase amount is greater than the average total paid purchase amount per customer.

```sql
SELECT
    c.Customer_ID,
    c.Customer_Name,
    SUM(p.Payment_Amount) AS Total_Purchase
FROM Customer c
INNER JOIN Orders o
    ON c.Customer_ID = o.Customer_ID
INNER JOIN Payment p
    ON o.Order_ID = p.Order_ID
WHERE p.Payment_Status = 'Paid'
GROUP BY c.Customer_ID, c.Customer_Name
HAVING SUM(p.Payment_Amount) > (
    SELECT AVG(Customer_Total)
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUM(p2.Payment_Amount) AS Customer_Total
        FROM Orders o2
        INNER JOIN Payment p2
            ON o2.Order_ID = p2.Order_ID
        WHERE p2.Payment_Status = 'Paid'
        GROUP BY o2.Customer_ID
    ) AS Average_Customer_Purchases
)
ORDER BY Total_Purchase DESC;
```

### 5. Advanced Business Report
Generate a product-wise report showing product details, units sold, paid sales, and comparison with the average product price. Products without paid orders are also included.

```sql
SELECT
    p.Product_ID,
    p.Product_Name,
    p.Category,
    p.Price,
    COALESCE(SUM(
        CASE
            WHEN pay.Payment_Status = 'Paid' THEN o.Quantity
            ELSE 0
        END
    ), 0) AS Units_Sold,
    COALESCE(SUM(
        CASE
            WHEN pay.Payment_Status = 'Paid' THEN pay.Payment_Amount
            ELSE 0
        END
    ), 0) AS Total_Paid_Sales,
    CASE
        WHEN p.Price > (SELECT AVG(Price) FROM Product)
            THEN 'Above Average Price'
        WHEN p.Price < (SELECT AVG(Price) FROM Product)
            THEN 'Below Average Price'
        ELSE 'Average Price'
    END AS Price_Comparison
FROM Product p
LEFT JOIN Orders o
    ON p.Product_ID = o.Product_ID
LEFT JOIN Payment pay
    ON o.Order_ID = pay.Order_ID
GROUP BY
    p.Product_ID,
    p.Product_Name,
    p.Category,
    p.Price
ORDER BY Total_Paid_Sales DESC;
```

## Concepts Used
- Single-row subquery with AVG()
- Nested subquery with MAX()
- Correlated subquery with EXISTS
- Derived tables
- Aggregate functions with HAVING
- CASE expression and COALESCE()
- INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN

## Expected Outcome
The queries identify products priced above the average, the highest-spending customer or customers, purchased products, customers spending above the average, and a product-wise business report. Only payments with status 'Paid' are counted as sales in the purchase analysis.
